From 2d6e87c7d87bbe5b2d96761ebdf55f18b479d171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 03:41:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 258/258] fix(cpu): bound the SVE256 ELF re-read and verify
 before every spawn

Round-2 verification of the 0044 memo hardening registered two more
boundaries:

* `_read_native_bytes` only wrapped `os.open`; `os.fstat`/`os.read`
  OSError and MemoryError escaped raw, and a sparse append made a memo
  hit read/allocate the whole file (probe_10: 1 GiB sparse under
  RLIMIT_AS=256 MiB -> raw MemoryError, memo entry retained).
* Non-W8A8 dispatch went from the launch decode straight to
  `_run_runner` with no re-check, so a rewrite in that window was
  executed by the child (probe_07).

`_read_native_bytes` now enforces a 64 MiB cap and, when known, the size
captured at decode time *before* reading; it reads into a pre-sized
buffer with os.readv, re-checks ino/size/mtime after the read, and
raises the canonical CpuSve256ArtifactError for every open/fstat/read
OSError, size/limit mismatch, short read and MemoryError.  A memo hit
drops the entry and falls back to the full decode on any of these, so no
raw MemoryError can escape and no stale entry can be reused.

Every runtime subprocess that executes the artifact (`_invoke_runner_raw`
and `guarded_buffer_self_test`) now re-hashes the on-disk ELF (0.45 ms)
immediately before spawning; a mismatch fails closed before the child
starts.  This mitigates probe_07.  The check->exec TOCTOU and the
unprivileged FUSE per-PID view split stay registered boundaries: both
need fd-based/private-copy execution rather than another read, which is a
runner/protocol change and out of scope here.

Same-window numbers on the 883,064-byte model ELF: miss 2.733 s, checked
memo hit 0.660 ms (4,140x), bounded read+hash 0.447 ms, pre-exec verify
0.450 ms.  W8A8 per-op times are unchanged within noise (5120: 19-28 ms,
30720: 44-70 ms, 65536: 76-132 ms) and the whole-graph QEMU smoke is
PASS at 70.9 s with bit-identical outputs.

Tests: sparse 1 GiB append under RLIMIT_AS=256 MiB (subprocess) stays
canonical with an empty memo; injected read MemoryError is canonical;
unreadable/directory/unlinked paths; probe_07-style non-W8A8 launch with
an injected malicious ELF raises before spawn and leaves no marker.
Three of the six new cases fail on the pre-round-2 code, so they pin the
fixes.
